    "raw": "\\*Data except enthalpy of formation at 298 K estimated. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 29.716 + 1.224x $10^{-3}$ T - 7.694x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o$ -  $H_{298}^o$  = 29.716x $10^{-3}$ T + 0.612x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 7.694x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 11.495</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -235.354 + 4.274 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 0.017 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 484.000 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -235.354 - 4.274 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln T - 0.017 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 242.000 \\text{T}^{-1} + 106.911 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Pankratz (92). ",
